"""Desk build packages for the in-house test rigs (AQS-TST-003, A-M-219): X-MFG-35 BMED bench stack and polarisation rig,
X-MFG-41 ZNBR2 10-cell stack rig hardware (procedure in AQS-TST-002), X-MAT-21 FRP coupon programme and load frame.
Sizes come from the plant designs (flow_graph/param/bmed_stack.py, drivers znbr_*), so the rigs test the plant duty.
The builds and tests themselves remain open (tasks stay unticked)."""
import json, math, os, sys
R = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))); os.chdir(R); sys.path.insert(0, R)
from flow_graph.param import bmed_stack, drivers as DR, solver
d, g, s = solver.solve(); v = lambda k: DR.val(d, k); b = bmed_stack.design()
# BMED bench stack
NT = 10; A = v('bmed_cell_area_m2'); j = v('bmed_j_A_m2'); I = j*A; Imax = 2*I; Vt = b['V_triplet_implied']; Vst = NT*Vt + 2.0
w = math.sqrt(A); vel = 0.05; gap = 0.8e-3; q_cmp = vel*gap*w*60000; q_loop = q_cmp*NT
naoh_g_h = NT*I*v('bmed_CE')/96485*40.0*3600
# ZNBR2
nc, Ac = 10, 0.1; jz = v('znbr_j_mA_cm2'); Iz = jz*10*Ac; Izmax = 40*10*Ac; Vz = nc*2.1*1.15
Ah = Iz*6; L_side = Ah/(2*26.8*0.5)*1.5
# FRP coupons
t = 6.0; Fmax_t = 400*13*t/1000; Fmax_f = 1.0
R_ = dict(bmed=dict(triplets=NT, I_A=I, Imax_A=Imax, V_stack=Vst, q_loop_L_min=q_loop, naoh_g_h=naoh_g_h), znbr=dict(I_A=Iz, Imax_A=Izmax, V=Vz, Ah=Ah, L_side=L_side), frp=dict(F_tensile_kN=Fmax_t))
json.dump(R_, open('docs-authority/inventory/TEST_RIGS.json', 'w'), indent=1)
md = ['# In-house test rigs: build packages', '', 'Document number: AQS-TST-003', 'Revision: A', 'Date: 2026-10-16',
      'Authority: AQS-PLAN-007 X-MFG-35, X-MFG-41, X-MAT-21. Generated by `docs-authority/_test_rigs.py`. A-M-219. Desk package: the rig builds and test runs are the open part of each task.', '',
      '## 1. BMED bench stack and polarisation rig (X-MFG-35)', '',
      f"Article: {NT}-triplet stack built to the plant cell (AQS-DUTY-068): {A*1e4:.0f} cm2 active ({w*1000:.0f} x {w*1000:.0f} mm) in {b['frame']}. Plant point {j:.0f} A/m2 gives {I:.1f} A; rig range to {Imax:.0f} A ({2*j:.0f} A/m2). Predicted stack voltage {Vst:.1f} V ({NT} x {Vt:.2f} V triplet + 2 V electrodes), so the supply is 0-40 V, 0-20 A, constant current, 0.1 % resolution. Predicted base output at the plant point {naoh_g_h:.1f} g/h NaOH.", '',
      '| Item | Specification | Qty |', '|---|---|---|',
      f'| Bipolar membrane, AEM, CEM | cut 300 x 300 mm to the frame gasket; {NT} BPM, {NT} AEM, {NT + 1} CEM (extra CEM at the cathode end) | {3*NT + 1} sheets |',
      f'| Flow frames and spacers | PP 300 x 300 mm, 0.8 mm PE woven mesh spacer, EPDM gasket, manifold ports per compartment (acid, base, salt) | {3*NT} |',
      '| Electrodes | Ti/MMO anode, 316L or Ni cathode, 300 x 300 mm with bus tab | 1 + 1 |',
      '| End plates | 25 mm PP with 8 x M10 tie rods, disc springs for 0.3 MPa gasket stress | 2 |',
      f'| Loops | acid, base, salt and electrode rinse (0.5 M Na2SO4); 5 L PP reservoir each; magnetic-drive pump 0-8 L/min ({q_loop:.1f} L/min at 5 cm/s in {NT} compartments) | 4 |',
      '| Instruments | conductivity x 3, pH x 2, Pt100 x 4, differential pressure across stack x 4, flow x 4; Pt voltage-sense wires at every triplet; Haber-Luggin capillaries with Ag/AgCl for one BPM | set |',
      '| Analysis | auto-titrator for HCl and NaOH product strength (CE by Faraday), ion chromatograph or titration for Cl- leakage into base | 1 |', '',
      f'Procedure: leak test at 1.5 x pump shut-off; conditioning 4 h at {j/2:.0f} A/m2; polarisation 25 to {2*j:.0f} A/m2 in 25 A/m2 steps, 5 min each, voltage per triplet; 8 h batch at {j:.0f} A/m2 with product titrated hourly; repeat at 40 C.',
      f"Measurements and acceptance: specific energy kWh/kg NaOH (plant basis {v('bmed_sec_kWh_per_kg_base')} kWh/kg, A-M-077), current efficiency (basis {v('bmed_CE')}), triplet voltage (physics {b['volt']['V_model']:.2f} V, design {Vt:.2f} V). The measured values replace bmed_sec_kWh_per_kg_base and bmed_CE and the plant re-sizes the stacks through the pipeline. Specific energy above 1.5 x basis is a design review.", '',
      '## 2. ZNBR2 10-cell stack rig hardware (X-MFG-41)', '',
      f"Procedure and acceptance are in AQS-TST-002. Hardware: {nc} cells x {Ac} m2; plant point {jz} mA/cm2 = {Iz:.0f} A, polarisation to 40 mA/cm2 = {Izmax:.0f} A; stack up to {Vz:.0f} V on charge.", '',
      '| Item | Specification | Qty |', '|---|---|---|',
      f'| Bidirectional cycler | 0-30 V, +/- 50 A, 0.05 % current accuracy, 1 Hz logging, Wh and Ah counters | 1 |',
      f'| Electrolyte | {L_side:.1f} L per side at 50 % utilisation of 2 M ZnBr2 for {Ah:.0f} Ah per 6 h charge; 10 L PP tanks with complexing-agent (MEP) phase separation | 2 |',
      '| Pumps | magnetic-drive, PVDF heads, 0-5 L/min, power metered (auxiliary energy) | 2 |',
      '| Thermal | chiller-heater 1 kW on a PVDF coil in each tank, 25 and 40 C set points | 1 |',
      '| Gas | 250 mL gas burette on the negative tank head space; H2 sensor at 10 % LFL alarm | 1 |',
      '| Safety | fume enclosure with extract, Br2 detector (alarm at 0.1 ppm), spill tray 110 % of both tanks, thiosulfate neutraliser on hand | 1 |', '',
      '## 3. FRP pultruded section coupon programme (X-MAT-21)', '',
      f"Coupons cut from the LEACH_CSTR_1 belt-channel section (pultruded web and flange), longitudinal (L) and transverse (T). Conditioning ASTM_D618_21 procedure A. Five valid specimens per test and direction.", '',
      '| Test | Standard | Geometry | Fixture | L + T + spare |', '|---|---|---|---|---|',
      f'| Tension: strength, modulus, strain | ASTM_D638_22 | Type I 165 mm, 13 mm narrow, as-pultruded thickness (Type III above 7 mm) | wedge grips, 50 mm extensometer | 5 + 5 + 2 |',
      '| Flexure: strength, modulus | ASTM_D790_17 | 16:1 span (32:1 if modulus > 20 GPa), width 13 mm, length span + 20 % | three-point, 5 mm loading nose and supports | 5 + 5 + 2 |',
      '| Short-beam shear (interlaminar) | ASTM_D2344_22 | length 6 t, width 2 t, span 4 t | 6 mm nose, 3 mm supports | 5 + 5 + 2 |',
      '| Density | ASTM_D792_20 | 1 to 5 g pieces | balance with sinker | 5 |',
      '| Liquor ageing (added) | the three tests above after 1,000 h in plant leach liquor at 77.5 C | as above | ageing tank | 15 |', '',
      f"Load frame: in-house screw-driven frame 50 kN (largest coupon {Fmax_t:.0f} kN at 400 MPa x 13 mm x {t:.0f} mm), load cell class 1 to ISO7500_1_2018, crosshead 1 to 500 mm/min. Allowable = mean - 2.0 s (five specimens) for strength, mean for modulus, after the ageing retention factor. The results replace the A-M-034 allowable, modulus and density.", '']
open('docs-authority/TEST_RIGS.md', 'w').write('\n'.join(md))
print(json.dumps(R_))
